            <div xml:id="d286">

                <pb facs="0302" n="298" xml:id="pg298"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/13948: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Hankow</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Josselyn</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Hankow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-09-23T14:00:00+08:00">September 23, 1938—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 7:13 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>My September 13, 7 p.m. regarding proposed Chinese defenses on oil company
                    installations.</p>
                <p>Mayor informed me orally this morning that Chinese military had decided not to
                    erect defenses on Standard Oil Company or Texas Oil Company property.</p>
                <p>Sent to Chungking.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Josselyn</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
